Welcome to StrataOS 0.1: a microkernel with preemptive multitasking.

Core 0 runs only the kernel. Files, the console, pipes, processes and
devices are servers (fs, tty, pipe, proc, dev): user processes that get
requests as lent message buffers. Programs share worker cores, switched
every 2 ms (`sched` shows and sets the slice); a switch saves only the
Local Store a program uses (ps shows the switches and the KiB they moved).

Try:
  ls                         programs, their sources and files
  tags, ls /src/demo         files carry tags instead of living in directories
  ls /src, ls /src/-demo     tags work as folders (demo/); -tag leaves one out
  cp, mv, touch, rm          copy, rename (mv f /todo/ adds a tag), create
  tag, untag, retag f t...   give a file tags, take them, replace them
  seq 30 | grep 2 | wc       a pipeline through the pipe server
  -n 3 mandel                a bare-metal program as 3 threads on 3 cores
  spin 20 a & spin 20 b &    time sharing (add -c 6 to put both on core 6)
  ps, cores, free, uptime    who runs where, and what switching costs
  as < hello.s > hi          assemble with the assembler written in Strata
  spin                       runs forever: press Ctrl-C to stop it
  ws                         the window server: tiled windows (help lists its keys)
  ping 127.0.0.1             TCP/IP: starts the network server; also nc, tcpecho, netstat
  httpd &                    web server: http://localhost:8080 (make boot)
